### Shelfly API — manual test requests
### Works with the IntelliJ HTTP Client or the VS Code "REST Client" extension.
### Run requests top to bottom: register/login first to get a token, then paste
### the token into the @adminToken / @memberToken variables below.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8082/api
@adminToken = PASTE_ADMIN_TOKEN_HERE
@memberToken = PASTE_MEMBER_TOKEN_HERE

### 1. Register a new member
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "test.user@shelfly.com",
  "password": "Password123!"
}

### 2. Login as seeded admin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@shelfly.com",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

### 3. Login as seeded member
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "email": "member@shelfly.com",
  "password": "Member123!"
}

### 4. Browse books (public, no token needed) — search + filter + sort + pagination
GET {{baseUrl}}/books?keyword=clean&category=Software Engineering&status=ACTIVE&sortBy=title&direction=asc&page=0&size=10

### 5. Get one book's details
# Replace {bookId} with a real id from response #4
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/{bookId}

### 6. Admin creates a book
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "title": "Refactoring",
  "author": "Martin Fowler",
  "isbn": "9780134757599",
  "category": "Software Engineering",
  "description": "Improving the design of existing code.",
  "totalCopies": 2,
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

### 7. Admin updates a book
PUT {{baseUrl}}/books/{bookId}
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

{
  "title": "Refactoring, 2nd Edition",
  "author": "Martin Fowler",
  "isbn": "9780134757599",
  "category": "Software Engineering",
  "description": "Updated edition.",
  "totalCopies": 3,
  "status": "ACTIVE"
}

### 8. Admin deactivates a book (soft delete)
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/books/{bookId}/deactivate
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 9. Admin deletes a book (only allowed if 0 copies on loan)
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/books/{bookId}
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 10. Member borrows a book
POST {{baseUrl}}/borrowings
Content-Type: application/json
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}

{
  "bookId": "{bookId}"
}

### 11. Member views their own borrowings
GET {{baseUrl}}/borrowings/my?page=0&size=10
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}

### 12. Member returns a book
# Replace {borrowingId} with an id from response #11
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/borrowings/{borrowingId}/return
Authorization: Bearer {{memberToken}}

### 13. Admin views all borrowings (optionally filter by status)
GET {{baseUrl}}/borrowings/all?status=BORROWED&page=0&size=10
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 14. Admin dashboard summary
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/summary
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 15. Report: most borrowed books (MongoDB aggregation)
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/most-borrowed
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 16. Report: borrowings by category (MongoDB aggregation)
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/by-category
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}

### 17. Report: overdue borrowings
GET {{baseUrl}}/reports/overdue
Authorization: Bearer {{adminToken}}
